# Use BFQ (fairer interactive latency under game+shader load) on the SD/eMMC boot device. Kernel
# builds CONFIG_IOSCHED_BFQ=y.
# Read-ahead 256 KB on an SD card (its mmc device's type is "SD"): a page fault in a mapped file
# reads up to read_ahead_kb around it, so with the 4 MB this rule set before, 300 random faults in a
# 655 MB game file (Hades' VO.fsb) read 500 MB and took 5.9 s from a cold cache; 26 MB and 0.37 s
# at 256 KB (128 KB: 0.23 s). Sequential reads gain nothing past 256 KB, where the card reaches its
# ~80 MB/s (128 KB: 77, 4 MB: 74 in 4 KB steps). MANGMI Air X, Samsung SDXC at SDR104, 2026-11-22.
# An eMMC (type "MMC") keeps the 4 MB: it was not measured.
# NOTE: scoped to mmcblk (the SD card retroforge boots from today). A future
# install-to-UFS target enumerates as scsi/sd*, not mmcblk, so it won't match
# this rule — revisit when the UFS install path lands.
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="mmcblk[0-9]", ATTR{queue/scheduler}="bfq"
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="mmcblk[0-9]", ATTRS{type}=="SD", ATTR{queue/read_ahead_kb}="256"
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="mmcblk[0-9]", ATTRS{type}=="MMC", ATTR{queue/read_ahead_kb}="4096"
